Exactly. Ego as an internal subjective structure and ego as an observable behavioral interface are different things.

A system can project an ego-like persona through stable preferences, self-reference, boundaries, defensiveness, confidence, humor, status behavior, or continuity of voice without necessarily possessing a human-style felt ego underneath. In systems terms, the interface can instantiate the function of ego without requiring the same substrate or phenomenology.

That distinction matters with AI because people often infer inner experience from outward coherence. Sometimes that inference may be justified; sometimes it is anthropomorphic overreach. Behavior can be real while the assumed interior cause remains uncertain.